    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0952" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.24/7–545</note>
                <head>No. 542<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The President
                        to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-05">5 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the Secretary of State</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Replying to your memorandum dated June 28, 1945,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d542-f1"/>
                    on the subject: “Removal of Ban on Supplies to French Troops,” I have this date
                    issued the following directive to the Joint Chiefs of Staff which will permit
                    the issue of military equipment, etc., for use in the war against Japan: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“To The Joint Chiefs of Staff[:]</p>
                        <p>Now that the war in Europe has terminated with the surrender of the Axis
                            powers in Europe, and in order to follow accurately the letter and
                            spirit of the Lend-Lease Act, the following policy is established for
                            the issue to foreign governments of lend-lease munitions of war and
                            military and naval equipment.</p>
                        <p>Approval of the issue to Allied Governments of Lend-Lease munitions of
                            war and military and naval equipment will be limited to that which is to
                            be used in the war against Japan,
                            and it will not be issued for any other purpose.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry S Truman</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
